    ['Application layer and client-server','In the city','An application defines the meaning of requests, responses and data. In client-server communication, clients request services from servers.','The ambulance originates the alert. The control center relays the message path and the hospital receives the emergency notification.'],
    ['DNS','In the city','DNS resolves names to records, such as addresses, so applications can use meaningful names.','The engine logs emergency-center.local resolving to 192.168.100.10 after a fixed delay. No actual DNS query is sent, and the .local name is only a teaching label.'],
    ['HTTP, APIs and the WWW','Concept only','HTTP describes request and response semantics. APIs expose application operations; the Web uses HTTP to exchange representations.','The engine logs an illustrative POST /api/emergency and HTTP 200 OK acceptance. The journey’s UDP alert is an abstraction, not an actual HTTP-over-UDP exchange. HTTP/3 uses QUIC over UDP; that is not modeled here.'],
    ['Peer-to-peer (P2P)','Concept only','Peers can exchange information directly instead of relying on one central application server for every interaction.','The retained engine has an illustrative ambulance-to-police message. The simple main journey does not expose a P2P control or implement a real vehicle radio protocol.'],
    ['Email','Concept only','Email commonly uses SMTP for sending and transfer, with IMAP or POP for mailbox access.','An emergency system might email a later report. This project does not send email or contact a mailbox.'],
    ['SSH','Concept only','SSH supports authenticated, encrypted remote access and related services over an insecure network.','Administrators might use SSH to manage equipment. This simulator has no remote terminal, SSH connection or device credentials.'],
    ['Emergency priority','In the city','Priority policies can distinguish urgent traffic from ordinary data when resources are shared.','Emergency alerts carry a CRITICAL label and a distinct packet shape; nearby traffic lights turn green visually. The engine does not implement a separate priority packet scheduler.']
